- The MCPX APU (native/dev/apu) is xemu's device, ported to the native core.
  Each of its files keeps the license its header states:
  - GNU Lesser General Public License, version 2 or later
    (licenses/LGPL-2.1.txt): apu.c, apu_debug.h, apu_int.h, apu_regs.h,
    debug.c, fpconv.h, dsp/dsp_dma.c, dsp/dsp_dma.h, dsp/dsp_dma_regs.h,
    dsp/gp_ep.c, dsp/gp_ep.h, vp/vp.c, vp/vp.h, vp/hrtf.h.
  - GNU General Public License, version 2 or later (licenses/GPL-2.0.txt):
    the DSP56300 emulator, adapted from Hatari's DSP M56001 emulation
    (ARAnyM developer team): dsp/debug.c, dsp/debug.h, dsp/dsp.c, dsp/dsp.h,
    dsp/dsp_cpu.c, dsp/dsp_cpu.h, dsp/dsp_cpu_regs.h, dsp/dsp_dis.c.inc,
    dsp/dsp_emu.c.inc, dsp/dsp_state.h.
  - GNU General Public License (licenses/GPL-2.0.txt): vp/svf.h, adapted
    from the SWH LADSPA plugins (Steve Harris), whose source names no
    version (svf_1214.xml: copyright "GPL"; xemu's header says GPLv2).
  - BSD 3-Clause (licenses/adpcm-xq.license.txt): vp/adpcm.h, the ADPCM-XQ
    decoder (David Bryant).
  The DSP JIT bridge (dsp/jit.c) is adapted from xemu and retains its
  GPL-2.0-or-later notice. The voice-processor port includes raddad772's
  work from https://github.com/xemu-project/xemu/pull/3105.
- native/kernel/xboxkrnl.exe.def comes from nxdk: CC0-1.0.
- native/libretro/libretro.h and libretro_vulkan.h are RetroArch's libretro
  API headers: MIT (licenses/libretro.license.txt).
- The window presenter's shaders (hw/xbox/hle/vk/swapchain.c): its FXAA is
  FXAA 3.11 Quality (Timothy Lottes) as PCSX2's fxaa.fx tunes it, GNU
  General Public License, version 3 or later; its SGSR is Qualcomm's
  Snapdragon Game Super Resolution 1, BSD 3-Clause
  (licenses/snapdragon-gsr.license.txt).
- License texts for dependencies are in licenses/. The versions used
  to build the core are pinned in tools/native/linux-deps.json.
